WEBVTT

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:34.480
There you go.

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:36.850
It's fine that you're going out to play,

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:39.060
but don't take your eyes off Sue-chan.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:41.530
Don't worry. We know.

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:47.870
Sue-chan's so tiny and cute, 
people always want to take her right away.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:51.070
Wait just a minute. What does that mean?

00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:54.740
Nothing.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:57.450
Don't hurt me!

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:00.480
Don't say things that sound so bad.

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:02.680
I've never hit you, have I?

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:04.150
No lectures, either!

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:06.880
That'll depend on you three.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:11.730
Well, see...

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:18.030
Mew!

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:24.770
You want us to rub your tummy?

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:27.460
Meow!

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:35.730
Sue-chan, want to rub him, too?

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:36.540
Meow...

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.100
Mew.

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:46.420
Want to go inside now?

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:53.140
M-Mew?

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:55.400
Meow, meow! Meow, meow!

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:56.180
Meow?

00:02:56.740 --> 00:02:57.780
Meow!

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:01.490
Move!

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:06.810
Now, Yoshi, Sue-chan isn't your doll.

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:09.110
Mew...

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:13.790
<i>I do seem to recall a time they 
came home smelling like dog...</i>

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:15.330
And? What else?

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:17.210
Well, um...

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:20.830
That's outside, this is inside.

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:23.090
So I can go this far.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:30.260
Sue-chan's gone!

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:32.890
Sue-chan!

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:35.270
Where are you, Sue-chan?

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:37.790
Where did you bring her from?

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:37.810
Nee-nee... Nee-nee...

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:38.770
She was lying around.

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:40.540
That way!

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:42.740
Sue-chan!

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:44.540
There she is!

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:47.690
Hey! You thief!

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:49.090
Give her back!

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:51.670
No! I found her!

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:53.940
She's my baby sister now.

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:56.440
No! Mew...

00:03:56.810 --> 00:04:00.060
Is she your little sister? I'm sorry.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:01.960
Now, let her go!

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:05.220
Nee-nee... Nee-nee!

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:06.550
I see.

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:11.720
So that's why the oldest Kawamoto sister 
is always apologetic toward me.

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:15.370
G-Good morning.

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:16.530
Morning.

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:18.790
Chi-chans!

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:21.530
We can go now, right?

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:22.490
Yes, you can.

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:25.500
Be sure you don't let 
her out of your sight.

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:27.490
We know.

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:33.420
<i>You say that, but I know you really won't.</i>

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:36.420
There...

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:39.380
Be home by dark, you two.

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:40.170
Okay.

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:42.420
Bye!

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:46.400
Going for a walk, going for a walk...

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:51.800
Nee-tan, Nee-tan.

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:54.970
There are all different kinds of grass,
 aren't there?

00:04:54.970 --> 00:04:56.300
That's right.

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:59.050
But they're all still grass?

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:01.310
No, not at all.

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:05.570
All the grasses in the field 
have their own names, too.

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:08.690
What about this fluffy one?

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:10.700
That's green foxtail.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.120
We call it "enokoro grass" in Japanese,

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:16.710
because it looks like the 
tail of a puppy (<i>inukoro</i>).

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:21.610
What about this one?

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:22.740
Indian goosegrass.

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:25.300
And this?

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.080
That's evening primrose.

00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:32.100
Not long ago, yellow flowers bloomed
 on them in the early morning.

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:34.580
Look at the little white flowers!

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:35.770
It's daisy fleabane.

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:37.740
Red flowers!

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:39.100
Red clovers.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:40.910
Sow thistle.

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:42.530
Creeping woodsorrel.

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:46.620
The boys play swords with these!

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:48.700
That's Canada goldenrod.

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:56.510
Do all the plants here 
have their own names?

00:05:56.510 --> 00:05:57.960
They do.

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:02.130
Even the smallest grasses 
and flowers have names.

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:18.090
This is called red clover.

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:20.180
Good, you remembered.

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:23.560
It has a name?

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:26.580
It's not just a red flower?

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:31.290
Yeah. Even the smallest grasses 
and flowers have names.

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:35.540
My name is Mi-chan.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:38.140
Shino-chan. Maki-chan.

00:06:38.140 --> 00:06:40.030
That's different!

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:51.200
You can have red blocks with some shaped 
like triangles and some like squares, right?

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:53.030
That's a triangle.

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:54.310
That's a circle.

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:56.380
That's right.

00:06:56.380 --> 00:07:00.070
Just like with blocks, 
flowers come in lots of shapes,

00:07:00.070 --> 00:07:02.120
and they all have names.

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:04.260
Like flowers?

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:09.030
But the triangle can be square, too.

00:07:11.690 --> 00:07:13.830
And the circle can be square, too.

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:18.150
Um, um...

00:07:18.150 --> 00:07:20.910
But the square block only has square sides,

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:24.840
and the circle has a circle side, and the 
triangle one has a triangle side, right?

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:28.330
Are there any that are only 
triangles or only circles?

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:31.240
One that's only triangles would be pointy,

00:07:31.240 --> 00:07:33.510
and one that's only circles 
would be a ball.

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:37.720
It's only a circle!

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:40.280
But you can't stack it 
if it's only a circle.

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:42.970
That's why blocks always 
have a square side.

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:49.070
There...

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:51.990
You don't have to try so hard...

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:53.110
There...

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:54.240
That looks kind of fun.

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:58.890
This purple flower is a kind of aster.

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:03.650
This has prickly leaves 
and pointy purple flowers.

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:04.990
They're thistles.

00:08:05.350 --> 00:08:07.240
They're not purple flowers?

00:08:07.510 --> 00:08:10.880
There are different purple flowers, 
like with triangle and circle blocks.

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:13.000
That's cosmos.

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:14.880
It has eight petals.

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:21.290
One, two, three, four, 
five, six, seven, eight.

00:08:21.670 --> 00:08:24.290
You're very good at counting.

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:26.400
Nee-tan, Nee-tan!

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:30.740
This is, um... red morning glory!

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:33.780
That's right, Maki-chan! Very good!

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:36.370
This is buckwheat.

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:37.400
Buckwheat?

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:41.850
Uh-huh. After it flowers, 
you pick the fruit and turn it into powder.

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:45.450
That's what they use to make 
the soba noodles you eat.

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:47.410
They're all white and cute.

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:51.420
Even smaller flowers than this
 have their own names.

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:52.790
Oriental lady's thumb.

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:56.420
See how it has lots of 
tiny red flowers on it?

00:08:56.730 --> 00:08:58.890
But there's no thumb.

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:03.420
Nobody knows why some of them 
are named the way they are.

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:04.680
Why?

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:06.850
<b>Plant Expert</b>

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:07.220
Someone came up with it a long time ago,

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:09.110
<b>Imperial University
 Doctor</b>

00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:09.420
and they told it to more and more people.

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:11.070
<b>Nee-tan</b>

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:13.220
Eventually, nobody knows how 
the name came about anymore.

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:15.870
The flowers have lots of little bumps.

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:16.970
Yeah.

00:09:16.970 --> 00:09:21.240
Some people use it as red rice 
when they play house.

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:24.990
That's why it's sometimes called 
a "red rice flower," too.

00:09:24.990 --> 00:09:27.000
You know so much, Nee-tan!

00:09:28.470 --> 00:09:32.590
My onee-chan taught me 
about this stuff, too.

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:37.360
So when both of you are old 
enough to be onee-chans,

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:39.410
teach it to some younger kids, okay?

00:09:39.410 --> 00:09:40.320
Okay!

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:46.670
Good morning, Miss Teacher!

00:09:46.670 --> 00:09:47.770
Good morning.

00:09:56.310 --> 00:09:58.010
Miss Teacher, this is awful!

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:01.730
The flowers are gone!

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:05.860
Oh, here? That's because we 
pulled up all the weeds.

00:10:06.090 --> 00:10:08.370
Who? Who pulled them up?

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:12.090
Maki-chan, first of all, 
put your fists down.

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:15.040
Nee-tan, it's terrible!

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:18.010
The flowers are all gone!

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:22.750
It's okay. The seeds are 
still there somewhere,

00:10:22.750 --> 00:10:25.750
so they'll flower again next fall.

00:10:26.990 --> 00:10:29.790
And before that, 
there'll be spring flowers,

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:32.770
and when they're gone, 
there'll be summer flowers.

00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:36.530
So when that happens, 
let's look at them together, okay?

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:37.510
Okay...

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:41.770
You make a very good older sister, Shino-chan.

00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:47.150
You saw us looking at the 
flowers yesterday, right?

00:10:47.380 --> 00:10:51.370
Huh? Well, but... It had to be done.

00:10:51.810 --> 00:10:54.470
I understand. It's grown-up stuff, right?

00:10:54.930 --> 00:10:57.380
I hope I get to be a grown-up soon, too.

00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:12.670
When all sides are triangles,
 it's called a triangular pyramid.

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:16.040
All of these pointed shapes 
are called pyramids.

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:18.410
One with a square bottom
 is called a square pyramid.

00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:20.640
One with a round bottom is called a cone.

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:23.450
Long ones with ends that are the same
 thickness are called prisms.

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:27.160
Round-ended ones are cylinders, 
and triangle-ended ones are triangular prisms.

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:30.560
Little kids ask all kinds of questions.

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:32.660
It's hard to be an onee-chan.

00:11:33.240 --> 00:11:37.450
You can't be good at it 
unless you study a lot.

00:11:37.450 --> 00:11:38.280
Huh?

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:43.040
But there are lots of things 
I don't know, too.

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:46.930
<b>There Are As Many Names of Flowers... 
As There Are People, But That's Totally a Lie!</b>

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:51.940
<b>There Are As Many Types of Beauty As There Are People, 
Which Is Probably True If Used in a Broad Sense?</b>

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:54.940
<b>Mitama</b>

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:03.950
<b>Mitama</b>

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:05.960
There.

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:13.810
Down, down...

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:17.450
Sue-chan, are you all dressed?

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:20.870
And there's your tail.

00:12:27.070 --> 00:12:30.080
I wanted to get dressed by myself.

00:12:30.780 --> 00:12:32.130
What's wrong?

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:37.040
Sue-chan couldn't get her tail 
through the hole in her outfit.

00:12:37.370 --> 00:12:38.460
Mew.

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:44.940
Okay then, today we'll have 
special tail training!

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:46.910
Training?

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:53.560
Now, do it just like I say, okay?

00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:54.290
Mew.

00:12:54.780 --> 00:12:56.930
Chi-chans, let's play!

00:12:56.930 --> 00:12:57.790
Okay!

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:01.920
Right.

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:04.360
Left.

00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:06.750
Middle.

00:13:07.610 --> 00:13:09.100
Down.

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:14.390
What are you all doing?

00:13:15.050 --> 00:13:16.830
Studying tails.

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:20.560
You're studying? That's very good.

00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:21.430
Mew.

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:23.610
Want to do it with us, Riri-chan?

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:25.690
What should I do?

00:13:26.730 --> 00:13:28.970
First, go from the right to...

00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:31.500
a circle.

00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:33.080
Meow?

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:34.700
Huh? A circle?

00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:39.950
Mew...

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:42.280
That's not much of a circle.

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:44.670
I don't think that's possible,

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:48.040
except for people with 
long tails like yours.

00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:52.760
Don't worry. It's okay if you 
can't make it a circle.

00:13:53.820 --> 00:13:55.620
Two circles.

00:13:56.410 --> 00:13:57.390
Meow?

00:13:57.390 --> 00:13:58.910
That's pretty good...

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:04.350
Meow!

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:08.040
Oh, hi there.

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:09.910
I came over to play.

00:14:14.300 --> 00:14:16.860
My tail is short.

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:18.820
That's okay.

00:14:18.820 --> 00:14:22.460
The Chi-chans' tails were short 
when they were little, too.

00:14:24.830 --> 00:14:27.080
See? They had tiny tails.

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:28.830
And flat ears, too.

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:31.720
Why were we dressed like that?

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:33.480
Tiny!

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:37.550
Back then, I was the one who 
always dressed you three.

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:45.310
But, Nee-chan...

00:14:45.990 --> 00:14:50.690
Wouldn't it have been easier 
to dress us in baby pants?

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:56.940
With pants and skirts, the tail 
has to go through two holes.

00:14:57.780 --> 00:15:00.080
Or you could just not put 
it though the hole at all.

00:15:00.430 --> 00:15:03.320
That wouldn't be very comfortable 
with pants, though...

00:15:07.120 --> 00:15:09.460
And it'd cause even more 
problems with a skirt.

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:15.000
With kimono, there's a way to wear 
them that keeps the tail inside,

00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:17.530
but it still has to go 
through a tail holder.

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:22.310
Then what about something like baby pants?

00:15:26.160 --> 00:15:28.800
The snap on those comes undone easily.

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:31.310
Remember when Sue-chan tripped 
and fell because of that?

00:15:34.570 --> 00:15:37.290
Either way, if you want your 
tail outside your clothes,

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:39.200
you need an undertag.

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:41.370
Undertag?

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:44.060
It's a loose piece of cloth inside a skirt.

00:15:44.870 --> 00:15:46.910
What are those for?

00:15:47.490 --> 00:15:50.300
Without it, if you moved 
your tail to the side,

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:52.560
your underwear would show through the hole.

00:15:53.210 --> 00:15:56.570
An undertag fills in the extra 
space so your underwear stays hidden.

00:15:57.150 --> 00:15:59.360
I don't mind if it shows a little.

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:01.380
Well, I do.

00:16:01.380 --> 00:16:03.470
But you don't even have a tail.

00:16:03.470 --> 00:16:05.970
I don't want your underwear to be visible

00:16:05.970 --> 00:16:08.270
to the kinds of people 
who'd want to see it.

00:16:09.370 --> 00:16:10.430
Nee-nee...

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:14.030
Were you little, too?

00:16:16.150 --> 00:16:19.090
When I was little, I looked like this.

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:21.880
Cute!

00:16:21.880 --> 00:16:23.730
Tiny Nee-nee!

00:16:24.090 --> 00:16:26.270
You looked just like Sue-chan.

00:16:28.810 --> 00:16:32.520
Why didn't you stay that cute, Nee-chan?

00:16:32.520 --> 00:16:34.250
I want to dress you up!

00:16:34.820 --> 00:16:36.390
If I'd stayed that cute,

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:40.010
I wouldn't be able to make 
you dinner or care for you.

00:16:41.010 --> 00:16:43.330
Everyone has to grow up.

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:48.510
Oh? You don't want dinner, then?

00:16:48.910 --> 00:16:51.200
We do need that!

00:16:55.070 --> 00:17:03.040
<b>World's Prettiest 
Person Contest</b>

00:16:56.540 --> 00:17:01.550
<i>Our next topic is the World's Prettiest 
Person Contest that was held recently.</i>

00:17:01.810 --> 00:17:05.260
<i>This "festival of beauty" 
began as a symbol of peace.</i>

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:05.230
What's that?

00:17:05.230 --> 00:17:07.280
It's about the prettiest 
person in the world.

00:17:05.260 --> 00:17:09.100
<i>This year's preliminary stage saw 
a record number of applicants.</i>

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:09.270
Prettiest?

00:17:09.270 --> 00:17:12.100
The prettiest in the world is Ma-nee-nee.

00:17:09.430 --> 00:17:14.520
<i>Thirty were selected from among them after 
careful screening of the applications.</i>

00:17:16.250 --> 00:17:17.380
Hey!

00:17:18.630 --> 00:17:20.780
No horsing around in the house!

00:17:22.550 --> 00:17:23.570
Nee-nee...

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:25.800
What is it?

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:28.820
What?

00:17:34.210 --> 00:17:37.650
You're the prettiest 
in the world, Nee-nee.

00:17:37.650 --> 00:17:38.780
What a good girl!

00:17:39.110 --> 00:17:41.280
Don't say that, Sue-chan.

00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:43.280
You'll give her a big head.

00:17:45.430 --> 00:17:47.620
There's always someone better.

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:51.050
Like, Nee-chan seems like the most 
important person in the world, right?

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:54.920
But there are even more important 
people in the world, like teachers.

00:17:55.310 --> 00:17:57.420
That's true. And your father.

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:03.820
I didn't say anything <i>that</i>
thought-provoking, did I?

00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:06.430
Dad is important?

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:09.190
He's the most important in this house.

00:18:09.610 --> 00:18:13.010
Anyway, there's bound to be 
someone prettier, too.

00:18:13.560 --> 00:18:16.040
Who do you think is prettier than me?

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:19.110
<b>Huh...?</b>

00:18:16.550 --> 00:18:17.470
Huh?

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:24.580
<b>Sakuraen</b>

00:18:38.520 --> 00:18:40.780
Wow! That was really good!

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:44.640
Are you all right?

00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:47.330
Don't be too reckless, okay?

00:18:49.570 --> 00:18:52.330
Miss Ryuko, you're very pretty.

00:18:53.060 --> 00:18:56.040
What's this? Are you trying
 to distract me with flattery?

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:03.410
But I still think our big 
sister is prettier.

00:19:05.280 --> 00:19:06.910
That's where this was going?

00:19:08.090 --> 00:19:09.950
So close...

00:19:13.320 --> 00:19:15.240
Don't be mad at them.

00:19:15.240 --> 00:19:16.770
I'm not mad!

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:21.300
I know I can't beat the pretty high school 
girl who's basically a mom to them.

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:36.860
I guess there aren't many 
pretty people around.

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:45.390
Shino-chan and her big onee-chans!

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:48.410
Hey, it's the class president's 
little shrimp sisters.

00:19:55.690 --> 00:19:56.640
There ya go.

00:19:59.060 --> 00:20:00.620
Pick me up!

00:20:01.090 --> 00:20:03.100
You three love attention, huh?

00:20:03.100 --> 00:20:05.090
Hey! Me, too!

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:06.940
Okay, okay.

00:20:11.470 --> 00:20:15.620
You're more cute than pretty.

00:20:15.620 --> 00:20:17.930
You'll be pretty someday.

00:20:18.580 --> 00:20:20.400
Nee-tan <i>is</i> pretty!

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:27.970
I bet you're a very pretty 
snake lady, Suu-chan.

00:20:27.970 --> 00:20:28.900
Are you?

00:20:29.250 --> 00:20:30.610
I'm not sure...

00:20:30.610 --> 00:20:33.370
Anyway, would you like me to pick you up?

00:20:37.090 --> 00:20:39.400
You're pretty too, Shino-chan.

00:20:40.240 --> 00:20:42.230
But you're still a kid.

00:20:42.230 --> 00:20:44.010
So are you!

00:20:44.630 --> 00:20:47.570
I get it. You're looking 
for pretty people, right?

00:20:50.070 --> 00:20:52.620
What do you think of her, then?

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:57.830
Do it more!

00:20:58.130 --> 00:21:02.150
You're a girl? I thought you were a boy.

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:05.110
Hey, you! Did you forget about
when we went to the pool?

00:21:07.470 --> 00:21:09.360
We're home!

00:21:11.480 --> 00:21:13.030
Oh, welcome home.

00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:17.560
I was about to go look for you, 
since it's getting dark.

00:21:18.600 --> 00:21:21.500
We looked really hard, too.

00:21:21.840 --> 00:21:22.800
For what?

00:21:23.330 --> 00:21:25.740
For someone prettier than you!

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:26.610
Find any?

00:21:29.250 --> 00:21:30.560
Nuh-uh.

00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:33.300
But it's a big world!

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:36.320
I'm sure there's someone prettier!

00:21:37.140 --> 00:21:39.810
Can't you just say I'm the prettiest
 and leave it at that?

00:21:40.110 --> 00:21:42.940
No! If you lose your drive 
to keep improving yourself...

00:21:42.940 --> 00:21:45.190
...you'll end up an old 
lady before you know it!

00:21:45.190 --> 00:21:50.430
By then, you three and Sue-chan 
will be the prettiest, so that's okay.

00:21:51.520 --> 00:21:53.060
We'll be pretty?

00:21:53.530 --> 00:21:56.300
If you're good girls and do as you're told.

00:21:56.970 --> 00:21:59.860
Why is there always a lecture involved?

00:23:31.970 --> 00:23:35.970
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:31.970 --> 00:23:35.970
<b>We Tried Making a Fantasy Story in RPG Style.</b>

00:23:31.970 --> 00:23:35.970
<b>Fierce Fights! Arm Wrestling! 
How Will the Battle of the Heroines End?</b>
